<title>AUSTRALIA: SOCCER-AUSTRALIA BEAT TAHITI 5-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-AUSTRALIA BEAT TAHITI 5-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia beat Tahiti 5-0</p>
<p>(halftime 3-0) in a World Cup Oceania zone second round, group</p>
<p>one qualifying match at Parramatta Stadium on Friday.</p>
<p>Scorers: Aurelio Vidmar 17, Paul Trimboli 39, 44, Graham</p>
<p>Arnold 46, Matthew Bingley 66</p>
<p>    Standings	   P   W   D   L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> Australia		2   2   0   0  18   0    6</p>
<p> Tahiti		   1   0   0   1   0   5    0</p>
<p> Solomon Islands	1   0   0   1   0  13    0</p>
<p>Next match: June 15, in Sydney, Solomon Islands v Tahiti.</p>
</text>
